<heading>grants path show - Show who has access to a path.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  show PATH
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Lists all subjects (accounts and groups) that have been granted
access to a specific runtime path, either directly or through
group memberships.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
show /usr/bin
  Show who has access to /usr/bin.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
account/show, group/show
</paragraph>
